import ../../helpers/driver.dl
import ../../../ui/text_popovers.dl

appearance background appearance:
    height is 280

appearance hint appearance:
    use UI text popover appearance
    maximum width is 200
    background is UI ink 245 247 249
    text is UI ink 25 30 35

document example:
    editor "Source" containing "kept" using no UI appearance
    (button "Behind the popover") wearing background appearance

set activations to 0
set {test viewport} to UI box at 10 10 sized 230 220
function [record background action] {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    globals:
        activations
    execute:
        increment activations

to get [read test popover] {a pointer:context} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    return read UI text popover (context as a pointer to UI text popover) in view

function [paint test popover] {a pointer:context} [on] {UI frame:frame}:
    globals:
        hint appearance
        test viewport
    execute:
        set style to UI appearance hint appearance resolved for (frame's view's width as a floating-point number) using (frame's view's instance's palette)
        paint UI text popover (context as a pointer to UI text popover) anchored at (UI box at 30 15 sized 10 18) within test viewport using (frame's view's typeface) styled style on frame

to [close test popover] {a pointer:context} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    clear UI text popover (context as a pointer to UI text popover) in view

set instance to an instance of example
set window to the address of instance
bind (the control labeled "Behind the popover" in window) in window to (the function named "record background action $") for event 0
set view to a UI view of window sized 400 by 300 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 1 key 0 at 5.0 10.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 2 key 1 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 2 key 0 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
set {editor source} to view's selection's caret source
set {editor caret} to view's selection's caret
require condition (view's input context's active) reporting "The popover fixture did not focus its source input."
set source to the string form of "First β😀 line wraps across this popover.\nSecond line."
set popover to a UI text popover containing source
set overlay to a UI overlay in (the address of view) with context ((the address of popover) as a pointer) handling input ((the function named "read test popover $ in $") as a pointer) painting ((the function named "paint test popover $ on $") as a pointer) closing ((the function named "close test popover $ in $") as a pointer)
set overlay's layout to the address of (popover's layout)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition ((popover's bounds' width = 200.0) and (popover's layout's text height > 30.0)) reporting "A text popover did not wrap its content to its declared width."
set x to popover's bounds' x + 13.0
set y to popover's bounds' y + 16.0
queue UI input of kind 1 key 0 at x y with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition ((view's selection's caret source = editor source) and (view's selection's limit = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text source))) reporting "Hovering a text popover stole the editor's text selection."
require condition ((view's hot = (the address of (popover's layout))) and (view's cursor shape = 2)) reporting "A text popover exposed its background control to pointer hover."
queue UI input of kind 3 key 262 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
process UI input in (the address of view)
require condition ((view's selection's caret source = editor source) and (view's selection's caret = editor caret + 1)) reporting "Hovering a popover captured the editor's keyboard navigation."
queue UI input of kind 2 key 1 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
process UI input in (the address of view)
require condition ((view's selection's caret source = (the address of (popover's layout's text source))) and (view's selection's dragging)) reporting "A popover could not own a text-selection gesture above another control."
require condition (view's input context's active = false) reporting "Selecting popover text retained the preceding editor input session."
queue UI input of kind 1 key 0 at -20.0 260.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 2 key 0 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
process UI input in (the address of view)
require condition ((view's selection's caret source = (the address of (popover's layout's text source))) and (activations = 0)) reporting "Dragging beyond a popover selected or activated its background."
queue UI input of kind 3 key 65 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 2 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 3 key 67 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 2 containing "" in (the address of view)
process UI input in (the address of view)
require condition ((view's window as a pointer to test UI surface)'s copied = source) reporting "Copying a wrapped popover included background text or changed its Unicode and line breaks."
dismiss UI text popover (the address of popover) in (the address of view)
require condition (view's selection's caret source = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text source)) reporting "Dismissing a popover retained its selection."
set run to view's texts
loop while run != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text run):
    require condition (run's source != (the address of (popover's layout's text source))) reporting "Dismissing a popover retained a borrowed text source in the preceding paint."
    set run to run's next
set UI text popover (the address of popover) to source in (the address of view)
set test viewport to UI box at 10 10 sized 20 20
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition ((popover's bounds' width = 0.0) and (popover's bounds' height = 0.0)) reporting "A popover painted content outside a viewport too small for its padding."
set test viewport to UI box at 10 10 sized 230 220
set view's damaged to true
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (popover's bounds' width = 200.0) reporting "A popover did not return when its viewport became usable."
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
close the address of view
close window
print line "Text popovers share wrapping, Unicode selection, scoped copying, input capture and source lifetime."
